--TEST--
Every class on the `RuntimeError` branch answers to exactly three of the tree's names — itself, `RuntimeError` and `Throwable` — so no sibling arm ever takes another sibling's throw — `rule:errors/throwable-hierarchy` and `rule:php-migration/one-type-test`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: TimeoutError
// One question asked of every class on the branch, answered by *counting*: a
// class that had quietly grown a second parent, or a sibling that had come to
// stand for another, passes every single-arm case in this directory and fails
// here.
class Branch {
    public static function names(Throwable $e): uint {
        uint $answers = 0;
        if ($e is Throwable) { $answers = $answers + 1; }
        if ($e is LogicError) { $answers = $answers + 1; }
        if ($e is RuntimeError) { $answers = $answers + 1; }
        if ($e is IOError) { $answers = $answers + 1; }
        if ($e is ParseError) { $answers = $answers + 1; }
        if ($e is TimeoutError) { $answers = $answers + 1; }
        if ($e is RecursionError) { $answers = $answers + 1; }
        return $answers;
    }
}

try {
    throw new TimeoutError("waited too long");
} catch (Throwable $timeout) {
    echo "timeout=", Branch::names($timeout), "\n";
}
try {
    throw new IOError("the disk is full");
} catch (Throwable $io) {
    echo "io=", Branch::names($io), "\n";
}
try {
    throw new ParseError("not a document");
} catch (Throwable $parse) {
    echo "parse=", Branch::names($parse), "\n";
}
try {
    throw new RecursionError("too far down");
} catch (Throwable $recursion) {
    echo "recursion=", Branch::names($recursion), "\n";
}

// The three a timeout answers to, named: itself, the half of the tree it is on,
// and the root. The other half is the one this must not answer to, and a
// `LogicError` arm written above the `RuntimeError` one below would take it if
// it did.
try {
    throw new TimeoutError("waited too long");
} catch (LogicError $ours) {
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $theirs) {
    echo "a RuntimeError arm takes it\n";
}

// A sibling's arm does not, and a sibling's arm is all that stands between this
// clause and the one below it.
try {
    throw new TimeoutError("waited too long");
} catch (IOError $sibling) {
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (ParseError $otherSibling) {
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (TimeoutError $itself) {
    echo "its own arm takes it\n";
}
--EXPECT--
timeout=3
io=3
parse=3
recursion=3
a RuntimeError arm takes it
its own arm takes it
